.TH "JSONKIT\-FETCH" "1" "" "jsonkit 0.0.0" ""
.SH "NAME"
jsonkit\-fetch \- Read one value at a path.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
\fBjsonkit fetch\fR <path> [options]
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Deprecated: Use get instead.
.SH "ARGUMENTS"
.TP
\fIpath\fR
Dot path to read.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-file\fR <\fIpath\fR>
The document to read. Omit it to read piped text.  (file or piped stdin, \- selects stdin; required)
.TP
\fB\-\-compact\fR
Print the JSON on one line.
.TP
\fB\-\-indent\fR <\fIspaces\fR>
Indent nested JSON by this many spaces, from 0 to 8.  (default: 2)
.PP
Use at most one of \-\-compact and \-\-indent.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBjsonkit\fR(1)
